docs {
  # Epic Games Store API
  
  Epic publish no third-party API. These requests use the Epic Games Launcher's own
  OAuth client (`launcherAppClient2`), the same one legendary, Heroic and Lutris use.
  Client id and secret are in `vars:pre-request` above.
  
  ## Getting authenticated
  
  1. Open https://www.epicgames.com/id/login?redirectUrl=https%3A%2F%2Fwww.epicgames.com%2Fid%2Fapi%2Fredirect%3FclientId%3D34a02cf8f4414e29b15921876da36f9a%26responseType%3Dcode
     and log in (legendary's short link https://legendary.gl/epiclogin redirects to the
     same place)
  2. The page body is JSON. Copy the `authorizationCode` value — it is not in the URL,
     and it expires within a few minutes and is single use. Note: refreshing the redirect
     page afterwards gives `"authorizationCode": null` — re-run the login link above for
     a new code, don't just reload
  3. Put it in `bruno/.env` as `EPIC_CODE`, then run "Get token"
  4. Copy `access_token`, `refresh_token` and `account_id` from the response into
     `EPIC_ACCESS_TOKEN`, `EPIC_REFRESH_TOKEN` and `EPIC_ACCOUNT_ID`
  
  Access tokens are short lived (hours). Re-run "Refresh token" rather than the whole
  login flow. Tokens are bound to the client id they were issued for.
  
  Secrets are read from a gitignored `bruno/.env`: copy `bruno/.env.example` to
  `bruno/.env` and fill in the values. Never commit `bruno/.env`.
  
  ## Notes
  
  - `artifactId` in the playtime endpoints is the library `appName` (== the catalog
    item's `releaseInfo[].appId`), not the `catalogItemId`.
  - The library endpoint returns identifiers only; titles and art need a catalog call
    per (namespace, catalogItemId).
  - Never call the playtime PUT endpoints — those write playtime to the account.
  
  ## References
  
  - https://github.com/derrod/legendary/blob/master/legendary/api/egs.py
  - https://github.com/Heroic-Games-Launcher/HeroicGamesLauncher/blob/main/src/backend/storeManagers/legendary/library.ts
  - https://github.com/lutris/lutris/blob/master/lutris/services/egs.py
  - https://github.com/MixV2/EpicResearch
  - https://github.com/LeleDerGrasshalmi/FortniteEndpointsDocumentation/tree/main/EpicGames/LibraryService
}
